12396	{"artifactId":"LLD-067b05b6892cb212-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-067b05b6892cb212-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-15T10:09:48.402Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every stated need of the Story: the declaration is read from the tool-call input rather than the tool-result output, the output-parsing path and the end-of-turn guess are removed, a name that is not pending has defined handling, and the steering text is updated.","evidence":"The Story's recorded need (memory turn-declares-documents.md) reads: 'a structured declaration read from the turn's tool-call INPUT …; remove the output-parsing path and the end-of-turn guess; decide what happens when a named document is not pending; update the steering text (src/prompts/steering-block.md)'. The LLD maps these to ac1–ac4. Section 2.1 drops toolResult and end-of-turn opening, 2.2 removes presentedPathOf, section 4 reports a not-pending name in the chat and in notPending, and migration step 4 rewrites steering-block.md. Rejected alternative a3 (a daemon ledger) is not built. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts, src/prompts/steering-block.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the presenter JSON-parses each tool result for a top-level pendingApproval.artifactPath, and at the end of a turn it opens whatever became pending since the turn began.","evidence":"review-presenter.ts:55-68: presentedPathOf calls JSON.parse(output) and reads parsed['pendingApproval']['artifactPath']. Lines 137-147: end() opens every doc for which `!state.before.has(doc.id)`. A non-JSON preview makes JSON.parse throw, and the function then returns undefined. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Codex mapper handles only command_execution and tool_call items on item.completed, so an mcp_tool_call item falls through unmapped; the tool-call event carries no input.","evidence":"cli-adapter.ts:752 has `if (itemType === 'command_execution' || itemType === 'tool_call')`. Any other item type reaches `emitAssistantText(turnId, text, state)` with an empty text (lines 779-781). The tool-call variant in stream-events.ts:33-49 has only tool, mcp, command and callId. The Codex branch never sets mcp. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/stream-events.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chat host feeds the presenter from two paths: the followed live turn and the hosted run.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:838-841: followLiveTurn calls beginPresented() on its first event, then presentResult(shown, ev). chat-panel.ts:1508 and 1551: runTurn calls `const shown = beginPresented()`, and the sink's onEvent calls presentResult(shown, ev). presentResult (line 813-820) currently passes only non-error tool-result events. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No workflow.pending wrapper exists in daemon-stream.ts, so a new one is needed. The MCP-side handler pattern (resolve the repo, then call a unary IPC) already exists and can be followed.","evidence":"daemon-stream.ts exports runWorkflowStream, startRun, pollRun, resolveRepoForCwd, approveWorkflow, abortRun, fetchCodeReview*, docgen*, guide* and review streams, but nothing for workflow.pending. server.ts:1099-1126 handleWorkflowApprove calls resolveRepoPath(args.repo) and then approveWorkflow(..., deps), which is the same shape the design proposes. [files: src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts, src/mcp/server.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chat's pending lookup in docs-review-client.ts is reused as it is and already drops records with no document file.","evidence":"docs-review-client.ts:133-140: pendingDocuments() calls 'workflow.pending' and returns `res.artifacts.filter((a) => typeof a.mdPath === 'string' && a.mdPath !== '')`. extension.ts:580-581 wires it into createReviewPresenter. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The real Codex capture pins the shape: mcp_tool_call with a bare tool name and an arguments object, emitted on both item.started and item.completed, with the completed item status failed.","evidence":"codex-mcp-tool-call.jsonl lines 4-5: {\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"mcp_tool_call\",\"server\":\"stub\",\"tool\":\"insrc_present\",\"arguments\":{\"documents\":[...]},...\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}, then item.completed with the same arguments and \"status\":\"failed\" (error 'MCP tool call requires approval, but approval policy is never'). The item type has no 'approval' in it, so the approval branch at cli-adapter.ts:730 does not take it. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fixtures/codex-mcp-tool-call.jsonl, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The golden tool-surface fixture holds twelve tools compared index by index after a name sort, so insrc_present belongs between insrc_guide and insrc_review_step, and the count and the test title change to thirteen.","evidence":"forward-step.test.ts:176-189 has the title 'the twelve tools …', `assert.equal(golden.length, 12)`, the surface sorted by localeCompare, and a per-index JSON compare. In tool-surface.golden.json, insrc_guide (line 426) is followed directly by insrc_review_step (line 441). [files: src/mcp/__tests__/forward-step.test.ts, src/mcp/__tests__/fixtures/tool-surface.golden.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"schema-registry.test.ts pins EXPECTED_TOOLS and PHASELESS_TOOLS, and asserts that the steering skeleton catalog names every tool, so the new tool must be added to both lists and to the catalog.","evidence":"schema-registry.test.ts:25 defines EXPECTED_TOOLS and line 54 defines PHASELESS_TOOLS. Line 58 asserts `[...schemaRegistry.keys()].sort()` equals EXPECTED_TOOLS. Line 134 asserts `skeleton.includes(tool)` for every expected tool, with the message 'the skeleton catalog should still name …'. [files: src/mcp/__tests__/schema-registry.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"steering-template.md only points at steering-block.md, so the approval text changes in steering-block.md, where the guide sections also live.","evidence":"steering-template.md:12 says 'The canonical block content lives in src/prompts/steering-block.md'. It contains no approval procedure. schema-registry.test.ts:110-120 shows readWorkflowGuide reads its per-workflow guide sections from that same steering asset. [files: src/mcp/steering-template.md, src/prompts/steering-block.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new present field is live-only. A tool-call event persists only as a marker row, so stored transcripts and old sessions are unchanged.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1700-1733 appendEvent: a tool-call event is written only as `{ role: 'marker', text: marker.label, cssClass: marker.cssClass, at }` through markerFor. No event field other than the label is stored. The existing callId field is documented the same way ('Live-only: never persisted into the transcript', stream-events.ts:44-47). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/stream-events.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An artifact id must be matched without regard to the case of its story part, because the daemon lists both -s1 and -S001 forms.","evidence":"The working tree has .insrc/artifacts/LLD-067b05b6892cb212-s1.json and LLD-370be5a6c8eee9c3-s1.json, so both casings exist on disk. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-067b05b6892cb212-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-370be5a6c8eee9c3-s1.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A not-pending name and an unreadable pending list can be shown as a line through the chat's existing information-line output.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:710 defines `const postInfo = (turnId: string, text: string): void`, which is used for live-only notes (lines 741, 2095, 2109, 2160). The presenter already catches read and open failures and logs them without throwing (review-presenter.ts:81-105), which matches the 'swallowed' error contract. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A declared repo-relative path resolves to the same pending document as an artifact id.","evidence":"The design states this as an edge case and has a unit test for it ('a declared artifact id and a declared path each open the matching pending document once'). The current samePath helper (review-presenter.ts:71-72) checks `presented.endsWith('/' + listed)`, where listed is the absolute mdPath, so it would not match a relative declared path. The rewrite must reverse that check (absolute listed path ends with '/' + declared path). The design leaves the matching rule to the implementation, and the named test covers it. The builder should note that the existing helper cannot be reused unchanged. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts]","action":"At build time, write the path matcher so that a repo-relative declaration matches the tail of the absolute mdPath; do not reuse samePath as it is.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1–ac4 maps to named tests. The suites the design rewrites (the presenter and chat-panel tests that pin toolResult and the end-of-turn open) exist and use node:test through tsx.","evidence":"Section 5's acceptance mapping lists proving tests for ac1, ac2, ac3 and ac4. The live behaviour (VS Code and Codex) is marked as live tests. chat-panel.ts:813-828 is the toolResult/end path those tests pin. The MCP-side tests (forward-step.test.ts, schema-registry.test.ts) are node:test files, as stated. [files: src/mcp/__tests__/forward-step.test.ts, src/mcp/__tests__/schema-registry.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-15T10:09:48.402Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
